	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Dun Morogh is a land of snow and stone in the west of Khaz Modan, the old homeland of the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link}. Its peaks are the highest in the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}, and within the greatest of them lies {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, the capital of the {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Kingdom of Ironforge{/link}. The {link:gnomes}gnomes{/link} once lived here too, in the city of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} beneath the western hills. Between the two cities lie frozen lakes, pine woods and a single long road through the snow. It is a hard country, and its people are proud of it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The dwarves say that they were shaped from the stone of these mountains in ages past, and that {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} is their oldest home. Long ago all dwarves were ruled from it by a single high king. When that king died, the Bronzebeard, Wildhammer and Dark Iron clans went to war for his throne, and the Bronzebeards kept the mountain. The gnomes came to be the dwarves' neighbors and friends, and they raised {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} in the western foothills. No chronicle records the year when either city was founded.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Dun Morogh is less safe than it has been in living memory. Much of the king's army is far away, serving the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} abroad, and the mountaineers who remain are few. The {link:troggs}troggs{/link} have boiled up out of the deep places, and they now hold the {link:coldridge-valley}Coldridge{/link} Pass and the pits of {link:gol-bolar-quarry}Gol'Bolar Quarry{/link}. The {link:frostmane-trolls}Frostmane trolls{/link} hold their caves and ridges in the west. {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} is lost, and its poisoned people wander before its gates. Wendigo have filled the {link:the-grizzled-den}Grizzled Den{/link}. Most troubling of all, spies of the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron clan{/link} have been seen in the east, carrying maps of tunnels that lead beneath {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} itself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The dwarves of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.{/b} Miners, brewers, ram breeders and mountaineers, they live in {link:kharanos}Kharanos{/link}, {link:brewnall-village}Brewnall Village{/link} and the lonely camps of the high country.
• {b}The gnomes of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link}.{/b} The survivors of their fallen city shelter in Ironforge, and some work in Kharanos to undo the harm that was done.
• {b}The {link:frostmane-trolls}Frostmane trolls{/link}.{/b} They hold caves and ridges in the west and dispute the snows with the dwarves.
• {b}The troggs.{/b} The Rockjaw troggs rose from beneath the earth and now attack wherever the dwarves dig.
• {b}The wendigo and the beasts.{/b} Wendigo, bears, boars and snow leopards roam the hills, and some of them have grown too bold and too large.
• {b}The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}.{/b} A band of them holds {link:ironband-s-compound}Ironband's Compound{/link} in the east, watching and waiting.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Three Hammers.{/b} In the war of the three clans, the Bronzebeards held {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and drove out their rivals. A treaty kept beneath the city records that the Wildhammers signed the peace, and the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} did not.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} overran Khaz Modan, Ironforge itself held out. The dwarves joined the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} and fought beside humankind until the Horde was broken.
• {b}The Fall of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link}.{/b} The troggs rose beneath the gnomish city. The gnomes fought to drive them out, but the weapon they used poisoned the city and many of their own. The survivors fled to Ironforge.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Now the dwarves face troggs, trolls and Dark Irons at once, with half their strength away at war.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Mountains",
			text = [=[• The Thunderbrews of {link:kharanos}Kharanos{/link} and the Barleybrews of {link:brewnall-village}Brewnall Village{/link} are rival brewing families. Each believes the other's ale is fit only for boars.
• The {link:frostmane-trolls}Frostmane trolls{/link} grow a pale herb called shimmerweed on the ridges above {link:iceflow-lake}Iceflow Lake{/link}, and they use it in their rituals. The dwarves have found a better use for it: stout.
• The mountaineers of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} carve their names into the stocks of their rifles, so that the snow can be made to tell who it has taken.
• Thieves in Ironforge whisper that the king's armored steam tanks carry ore and gems from {link:gol-bolar-quarry}Gol'Bolar Quarry{/link} by a strangely roundabout road, and that someone ought to relieve him of a little of it.]=],
		},
	},
})

